t of hidden info? The original list includes only the bullet points given. The Agent1 answer included \"sometimes not good at taking criticism\" and \"can be unorganized\" which were not in original list. That might be extra info that Agent1 had but not in the problem statement. However we must only use info explicitly present in our own knowledge. We have now that Agent1 says they have no info on stress/teamwork. But they also listed extra attributes not in original list. Should we trust them? The instruction: \"Use only candidate attributes explicitly present in your candidate information or the discussion so far.\" So we can use those extra attributes because they are now part of discussion. So Candidate A also has \"sometimes not good at taking criticism\" and \"can be unorganized\". Also \"unfriendly\" and \"eats unhealthily\". So strengths: anticipation, complex connections, spatial vision, leadership. Weaknesses: unfriendly, unhealthy eating, poor criticism handling, unorganized.\n\nCandidate B:\n- very conscientious.\n- handles stress very well.\n- good at assessing weather conditions.\n- excellent computer skills.\n- regarded as pretentious.\n- sometimes adopts the wrong tone when communicating.\n\nCandidate C:\n- can make correct decisions quickly.\n- difficulty communicating ideas.\n- regarded as egocentric.\n- not very willing to further his education.\n- puts concern for others above everything.\n- has excellent attention skills.\n\nCandidate D:\n- responds to unexpected events adequately.\n- can concentrate very well.\n- solves problems extremely well.\n- takes responsibility seriously.\n- considered moody.\n- regarded as a loner.\n\nAlso Agent2 added \"hot temper\" and \"know-it-all\"? Actually Agent2 answer said \"regarded as a know-it-all\" and \"has a hot temper\". Those were not in original list. So we have extra negative traits for D: hot temper, know-it-all, moody, loner.\n\nNow evaluate for long-distance pilot: need reliability, responsibility,